    "title": "Mick Cronin buyout, contract details as UCLA Bruins coach",
    "text": "Mick Cronin buyout, contract details as UCLA Bruins coach originally appeared on The Sporting News. Add The Sporting News as a Preferred Source by clicking here.UCLA boosted its commitment to men’s basketball coach Mick Cronin last May, approving a two-year contract extension that significantly raised his salary and buyout protections. But now many are wondering if that was a bad investment. Under the revised deal, which was first reported by the Los Angeles Times, Cronin will be under contract until at least 2023. This went unannounced by the university and was an uncommon move for a public institution overseeing a high-profile program.AdvertisementCronin now earns $4.5 million annually before bonuses. The extension also dramatically increases his financial protection. Under his previous agreement, he had $10 million guaranteed if terminated without cause. The updated contract more than doubles that figure.Mick Cronin's buyout termsIf UCLA fires Cronin without cause before April 1, 2026, the school would owe approximately $22.5 million. The buyout drops to $18 million before April 1, 2027, $13.5 million before April 1, 2028, $9 million before April 1, 2029, and $4.5 million before April 1, 2030. Cronin is signed through March 31, 2030.Given the escalating buyout structure, a potential dismissal would present significant financial hurdles, particularly amid broader athletic department pressures, including NIL commitments and revenue uncertainties.If Cronin leaves for another job, his buyout obligations to UCLA would begin at $15 million before April 1, 2026, decreasing incrementally to $4 million in the final year of the contract.The agreement includes a mitigation clause, reducing UCLA’s financial responsibility if Cronin secures comparable employment.AdvertisementMick Cronin's incentivesWith multiple incentives built into the contract, his yearly compensation is expected to surpass $5 million. Among the retention bonuses: Cronin receives $500,000 if he remains UCLA’s coach on April 15, 2026. That figure increases to $600,000 in 2027 and $700,000 in both 2028 and 2029 if he remains employed by the university.Cronin has led the Bruins to the NCAA tournament in four of the past five seasons. He's enjoyed success with a Final Four run in 2021, along with back-to-back Sweet 16 appearances. However, the welcome seems to have been worn out as of late. Cronin's conduct has questioned if it's time to move on. Especially after ripping a reporter and ejecting his own player in recent games.More college basketball news:",
